course: dictionary
lesson: 2906
title: A downpour of rain, or of anything
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A downpour is a very heavy rain that falls suddenly, often all at once. When you meet a new word, read the words around it. Clues like heavy and sudden tell you a lot before you check a dictionary.
explain: Writers also use downpour in a second way. A downpour of questions means a lot of questions arriving at the same time. You can spot this when the sentence is about something other than weather.
explain: «A warmer climate makes heatwaves more common, dries the ground faster and, because warm air holds more water, can make heavy downpours heavier.» Here the downpours are weather, so the sentence tells you the rain is extreme. Try swapping in very heavy rain. If the sentence still makes sense, you have the right meaning.
fact: A downpour is a very heavy fall of rain that comes down suddenly.
fact: Downpour can also mean a lot of something arriving at once, such as a downpour of questions.
fact: Phrases you may see include sudden downpour, heavy downpour and caught in a downpour.
fact: «Caught in a downpour» means you were out in heavy rain and got soaked before you could find shelter.
fact: In the example «heavy downpours heavier», the word heavy tells you the rain is very strong.
exercise: «We were caught in a sudden downpour on the way home.» What is a downpour? | *A very heavy fall of rain that comes down suddenly | A small puddle left after school | A gentle breeze on a warm day | A rainbow after the sun comes out
exercise: The teacher said, «We got a downpour of homework today.» What does downpour mean here? | A single sheet of paper | Homework that is wet from the rain | *A lot of homework arriving all at once | Homework that was lost on the bus
exercise: In «heavy downpours heavier», which word tells you the rain is strong? | ground | warmer | climate | *heavy
test: Which phrase means rain falling very hard, all at once? | Warm sunshine | Light breeze | Gentle drizzle | *Sudden downpour
test: Mia says a downpour is a small shower. Is she right? | Not sure, it has nothing to do with rain | Yes, a downpour is a small shower | *No, a downpour is very heavy rain that falls suddenly | Yes, it is the same as a drizzle
exam: In «He received a downpour of messages after the game», what does downpour most likely mean? | Messages that were lost in the post | Messages written in the rain | *A large number of messages arriving at once | A few messages sent slowly
